    {
      "path": "runtimes/codex/app-server-client.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/runtimes/codex/app-server-client.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "c48cdcff3f73ec7e35a5932ae8f72f5377f60e522f36b8a83b2bc4e3aee442bc",
      "vendoredSha256": "3b6fe43db538148350d3ac219e9a143c44c311443f15b0301b9c18acdf2e215e",
      "delta": "Caller-owned process: the injected LineProcess spawn receives exactly the explicit filtered env, cwd and launch arguments; no ambient env merge, home-initialization queue, executable manager, resources reader or killTree option. Server requests: numeric and string ids preserved; result and error replies go through the acknowledged stdin write. Terminal state: an exit or a kill sets one sticky terminal error, with the bounded, redacted exitError of the BYOK transport plus the upstream cleanup reason on exit; it settles every pending request as exited at once, rejects later requests and writes, and ignores later lines. No per-request deadline and no count budget: operation deadlines live in the SDK Codex adapter, and the BYOK transport bounds line bytes."
    },
