    {
      "path": "shared/acp/process.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/shared/acp/process.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "88918784e4c127fa3eeffb709fc33daad833b5bf91900e5586e1edbc2df2418b",
      "vendoredSha256": "26e51e155146e3f3c8ad38803916b3e236ae5b4949ec228695f3cc3adf7a9bcc",
      "delta": "Caller-owned process: startAcpProcess takes an injected SpawnAcpLineProcess and passes exactly the explicit filtered env and cwd; no executable manager, killTree option, resources reader or native diagnostics. The owned process splits stdout into bounded lines; each line goes back to the official ndJsonStream with its newline, and each written message goes through the acknowledged stdin write, so the SDK keeps its own framing, parse-error answers and write order. Upstream incoming/outgoing filters and the draining-EOF input are retained around the injected streams. No prepareShutdown, markNativeStop or observeCancellation members. Instead the injected line process and AcpProcess carry one synchronous observeDescendants(): the SDK process-tree authority reads the process table and remembers the agent's descendants for its disposal, and throws when the table cannot be read."
    },
