      "path": "shared/acp/session.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/shared/acp/session.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "5facb21e16f5df5d9a880300d6dcd5aafd5f122ee760cfd5932014418e3d3f6c",
      "vendoredSha256": "7116d4fde54e36946103e543d64ae174a734e443b61974398ebb481ffc2ad239",
      "delta": "Raw adapter for the SDK: acpSession(profile) returns a start function that takes the injected agent-process spawn, the injected terminal spawn and a required explicit filtered env (no sessionEnvironment ambient merge). It returns AdapterSession without sealSession/withSessionCredentials, does not use the upstream shared-connection pool or lifecycle wrapper, builds one sessionCredentialRedactor per open as the kernel redact hook and for errors from the open path and every control, and takes onReady and onRecord hooks; onRecord is registered as a kernel observer before the recorder binds. A throwing onReady releases the process and the terminal host. The exit observer terminal disposal is the same one dispose awaits, and a repeated dispose retries a failed terminal reap. No resources reader. Dispose does not call prepareShutdown or markNativeStop, and control does not wait on a pending cancellation observation. Upstream configUpdates, manual compaction and the adapter-held queue are wired in; compact goes through the redaction guard. endTurnProcessesOnAbort and retainedBytes are omitted from AcpSessionOptions."
    },
    {
      "path": "shared/acp/terminal.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/shared/acp/terminal.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "e6033c17a35bf85c3f05f380da102c3bb61838e86af4f2cb80d0b3f1da60da7e",
      "vendoredSha256": "b71a1f2496ca5b25504286782086826dd265bb173adb531114addcf45627760a",
      "delta": "Caller-owned terminal processes: createAcpTerminalHost takes an injected SpawnAcpTerminal that spawns, adopts and reaps each hosted command in the SDK process-tree authority with the session's explicit env plus the request's env entries. terminal/kill asks that tree to stop; release and dispose end the tree and wait for it. A released or disposed terminal stays tracked until its tree is gone. One disposal serves concurrent callers; a failed reap rejects and a later dispose retries every tree still alive. A terminal/create after disposal began is refused. No cross-spawn and no executable manager."
    },
    {
