      "delta": "Failed-prompt settle: a rejected session/prompt yields one event-loop turn before it reads its turn frames, so a notification from the same pipe read (grok's retry_state) is recorded first and the failure reader sees it. The success path already yields in promptAcp. abort has no upstream observation window (pendingCancellation is absent): it calls runtime.observeDescendants() synchronously before the native cancel, so a tool the cancel orphans stays known to the SDK process-tree authority, which kills it at dispose while it is the same process. A failed read rejects the abort with code error and sends no cancel."
